      "latency_ms": 2668.8,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 673,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound made up of two elements: **hydrogen** and **oxygen**. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**, meaning every single molecule of water consists of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom. \n\nHowever, water is much more than just a chemical formula. It is one of the most abundant, unique, and essential substances in the universe. Here is a breakdown of what water is through different lenses:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Physical and Chemical Properties\nWater is famous for being delightfully weird compared to other liquids. \n* **The Three States:** Water is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states: **liquid** (water), **solid** (ice), and **gas** (steam or water vapor).\n* **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Because of the way its molecules are shaped (with a slight positive charge on the hydrogen side and a slight negative charge on the oxygen side), water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it carries nutrients through our bodies and minerals through the earth.\n* **Density Anomaly:** Almost all liquids shrink and become denser when they freeze. Water does the opposite—it expands and becomes *less* dense when it turns to ice. This is why ice floats. If ice sank, lakes and oceans would freeze from the bottom up, destroying aquatic life.\n* **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before its temperature changes significantly. This is why oceans help regulate the climate of the entire planet, and why sweating cools our bodies down.\n\n### 2. The Essence of Life\nBiologically, water is the cradle of life. \n* **Life Needs It:** Every known form of life requires water. It provides the medium in which the metabolic and cellular processes of life take place.\n* **Our Bodies:** The human body is made up of about 60% water. Our brains are roughly 73% water, our lungs about 83%, and even our bones are about 31% water. We can survive weeks without food, but only a few days without water.\n\n### 3. Earth's Life Support System\nOften called the **\"Blue Planet,\"** Earth's surface is about 71% water. \n* **Distribution:** The vast majority of Earth's water (about 96.5%) is saltwater in the oceans. Only about 2.5% is freshwater, and most of that is locked away in glaciers, ice caps, or buried deep underground. Less than 1% of Earth's water is easily accessible for human use in lakes, rivers, and soil.\n* **The Water Cycle:** Water is constantly recycled through the **hydrologic cycle**. It evaporates from the oceans, rises into the atmosphere to form clouds, falls back to earth as rain or snow, and flows through rivers back to the sea. The water you drink today is the exact same water that dinosaurs drank millions of years ago.\n\n### Summary\nWater is a simple molecule with profound responsibilities. It is the solvent of life, the sculptor of landscapes, the regulator of Earth's climate, and the literal fluid that keeps living things alive."
